Explanation of 20% threshold:
20% frequency ratio: 1200 * log2(1.20) = 315.64 cents = 3.16 semitones.
Why exclude gross errors from fine-cent statistics?
An octave error (2x) is 1200 cents! If included, a single octave error would distort the mean cent error from 22 cents to hundreds of cents, hiding the true precision of the fine interpolation algorithm.
